elan: wait longer for the sensor calibration

The calibration status goes 0x03 -> 0x01 -> 0x03 and the driver checks it every 50 ms. Some
sensors (04f3:0c4f in the Acer Aspire 7 A715-42G) are still at 0x01 after 10 checks (measured: 4-19 checks, up to 1 s), so every
enroll and identify fails with "Calibration failed!". 0x0c58 already needed 30 checks; allow 100
(5 s) for all sensors - the limit only matters while a calibration is running.

--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
@@ -46,9 +46,8 @@
 
 /* times to retry reading calibration status during one session
  * generally prevents calibration from looping indefinitely */
-#define ELAN_DEFAULT_CALIBRATION_ATTEMPTS 10
-#define ELAN_CALIBRATION_ATTEMPTS(dev_type) \
-  ((dev_type) == ELAN_0C58 ? 30 : ELAN_DEFAULT_CALIBRATION_ATTEMPTS)
+#define ELAN_DEFAULT_CALIBRATION_ATTEMPTS 100
+#define ELAN_CALIBRATION_ATTEMPTS(dev_type) ELAN_DEFAULT_CALIBRATION_ATTEMPTS
 
 /* min and max frames in a capture */
 #define ELAN_MIN_FRAMES 7
